## 5. Why Didn't the Charge Bug Fix + 256-History Make `SOUL` an Easy >50%?

It is completely natural to feel frustrated here—you fixed the charge reset rules and expanded the network to 256 inputs so it can read match history, yet `SOUL` is still a tough wall to crack. Here is why that happens:

1. **Every Engine Fix Upgrades `SOUL` Instantly (at 0 Games), While the Network Must Learn It from Scratch:**
   * `SOUL` isn't a static script—it runs deep lookahead simulations using the live game rules. The moment you fixed `charge1-reset1` (preserving charge on same-direction repeats and resetting to 1% on direction switches), **`SOUL` immediately gained 100% mathematical mastery of charge-clock manipulation**.
   * Meanwhile, your neural network had to throw away all old 136/16 checkpoints and learn a much larger **256-input state space** from zero.
2. **256 Inputs Have Higher Capacity, Which Means a Longer Early Learning Curve:**
   * Reading multi-round history and charge states (256 inputs vs. 136) gives the network a much higher ceiling, but it also means there are more input weights to calibrate.
   * Your `001_003` model has only played **4,607 games** (one-fourth of the 18,561 games on `001_002`). Reaching **85% Easy / 54% Balanced (pure matrix) / 70% Master (RIDER)** in only 4,607 games is actually ahead of the old schema's pace!
3. **Why Raw `network` Hits a Wall Against `SOUL`:**
   * As noted in the build spec: *"The 17 outputs represent move keys, not charge percentages... Direct-network training uses a canonical reachable charge. RIDER evaluation preserves the search-selected charge."*
   * When `network` plays `SOUL`, `network` is forced to use a single fixed canonical charge %, while `SOUL` is micro-adjusting its charge between 1% and 100% to beat your canonical charge by 1 priority step. Only **`RIDER` evaluation** (and the actual live game engine, which gives the model even more thinking time) unlocks variable charge % to fight `SOUL` on equal footing.

---

## 6. Recommended Next Steps to Finalize `001_003`

1. **Evaluate `SOUL` Using `RIDER — live search policy` (20–30 Matches):**
   Since your raw matrix (`network`) **already passed `NOVICE` (85%) and `BALANCED` (54%)**, you only need `RIDER` for `MASTER` (already **70%**) and `SOUL`. Make sure your `SOUL` evaluation is set to **`RIDER — live search policy`**, not `Direct network`.
2. **If `RIDER` vs. `SOUL` Is Still Just Under 50%:**
   * Run **2,000–3,000 more training matches** on `001_003` (bringing it from `4,607` to `~7,000` games).
   * Keep **`Only winning matches update candidate` UNCHECKED** and set **`Guidance %` around `15%–20%`** against `SOUL` or `MIXED` so the network calibrates its defensive Q-values (`S+K` and `S+I` counters) against `SOUL`'s favorite lines.
   * Once `SOUL` crosses **$>50\%$**, click **ACTIVATE SELECTED CANDIDATE** and export it to `/data`—with the live game's extra move-calculation time, this `001_003` checkpoint will be brutal against human players.
